{"title":"Boolean lattice","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Given any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the <b>boolean lattice</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b7492fdbab2a1295cc0cccb3a143feb64e47e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partially_ordered_set\" title=\"Partially ordered set\">partially ordered set</a> whose elements are those of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51deaac5e024665f8d409987d79bf82bf618f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_set\" title=\"Power set\">power set</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, ordered by inclusion (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6ffbe0cb0b8d47bd10eec85fb336adf7694f896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\subset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />).\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Finite\" title=\"Finite\">finite</a> number of elements (say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/668f9177dad602e1de8c7b66f924b7ed6ae42119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S| = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />), the boolean lattice associated with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is usually denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be2b1de79fff66db67de3b18303bdd2912b7ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a2930bcc6c4f4638d4dedac498f70c7ca3b349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> is associated with the boolean lattice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48424701a2c36b4d4d6956d8c41e2798d8b32a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> with elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b37562bb004f993530d4f42a8c78f3b60391420d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\emptyset, \\{1\\}, \\{2\\}, \\{3\\}, \\{1, 2\\}, \\{1, 3\\}, \\{2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"271\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/62511f4d99c1621775385afa593225a56e41f220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, among which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/84241c448cbf497968ba86136beecf766431a3ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" /> is smaller than all others, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a2930bcc6c4f4638d4dedac498f70c7ca3b349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> is larger than all others, and the other six elements satisfy the relations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54a40eeab23e1c9b1f9994c50323279d40b9dea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1\\}, \\{2\\} \\subset \\{1,2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fb7ec6b96ab07a6cbd7c5c79581edba26091e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1\\}, \\{3\\} \\subset \\{1,3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a8eed58fc4b1991a7aee6d360b1102c23687a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2\\}, \\{3\\} \\subset \\{2,3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> and no others.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hasse_diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Hasse diagram (page does not exist)\">Hasse diagram</a> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48424701a2c36b4d4d6956d8c41e2798d8b32a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is given below:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Boolean_lattice&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Every boolean lattice is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distributive_lattice&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Distributive lattice (page does not exist)\">distributive lattice</a>, and the poset operations <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Meet&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Meet (page does not exist)\">meet</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Join&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Join (page does not exist)\">join</a> correspond to the set operations <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Union\" title=\"Union\">union</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intersection\" title=\"Intersection\">intersection</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Boolean_lattice&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235227\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 70/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 636/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3473/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.525      1 -total\n 70.79%   12.406      1 Template:Image\n 28.53%    5.000      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3983:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235227 and revision id 25084. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}